Negative control for the arm's re-ask being SCOPED (`AC8.4` · `R6-10`).

Drops the whole query cache on every arm and disarm, not just what the handlers
answer. The app chrome's own queries — the brand, its settings, the session — are
booted once at init by singletons that never re-ask, so the header is left holding
an undefined brand for the rest of the tab's life: the broken logo the live drive
found over every forced page.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the forced-state spec — reconciling a preset resets the module's own queries
and leaves every other domain untouched.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/composables/useForcedState.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/composables/useForcedState.ts
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/composables/useForcedState.ts
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/composables/useForcedState.ts
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
     // awaited for the same reason: a chain waiting on that refetch could never
     // reconcile the preset picked after it. Scoped to what the handlers answer:
     // the whole cache is the app's too, and the chrome does not re-ask.
-    void queryClient.resetQueries({ queryKey: MODULE_QUERY_KEY });
+    void queryClient.resetQueries();
